Subject: avoid delayed profile catch-up after suspend

Local fix against hyprsunset v0.3.3; not an upstream backport.
Upstream issue: https://github.com/hyprwm/hyprsunset/issues/55
Earlier workaround: https://github.com/hyprwm/hyprsunset/pull/59
Merge: 72071709f58bc2fed8546288af295aa9153a287f

PR #59 added the one-minute polling loop, limiting the delay without
eliminating it. The v0.4.0 scheduler still has that loop and sleep_until;
a version bump to v0.4.0 alone does not replace this patch. Reassess the
scheduler and CMake test wiring when updating the pinned package.

Use an absolute realtime deadline and preserve profile selection after
it expires. Native timer tests pass; physical suspend/resume acceptance
has not been performed. On a non-EINTR wait error, automatic scheduling
stops until restart while the daemon and manual IPC remain available.

